### Employees API Documentation
### Complete API documentation for employee management endpoints
### All operations for creating employees and employee login

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@contentType = application/json
@token = your-jwt-token-here
@employeeId = your-employee-uuid-here
@roleId = your-role-uuid-here

### ============================================
### VARIABLES SETUP
### ============================================
### Replace the variables above with actual values:
### - @token: JWT token from employee login
### - @employeeId: UUID of an existing employee
### - @roleId: UUID of an existing role (required for creating employees)

### ============================================
### 1. CREATE EMPLOYEE
### ============================================
### Create a new employee account
### Requires roleId to be a valid UUID of an existing role
### Email and phone must be unique
### Password is stored as plain text (as per current model implementation)

POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "phone": "+1234567890",
  "address": "123 Main Street, City, Country",
  "roleId": "{{roleId}}"
}

### Example: Create Employee with FCM Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Jane Smith",
  "email": "jane.smith@example.com",
  "password": "securepassword",
  "phone": "+9876543210",
  "address": "456 Oak Avenue, City, Country",
  "roleId": "{{roleId}}",
  "fcmToken": "fcm-token-for-push-notifications"
}

### Example: Create Employee by Another Employee (with createdById)
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Bob Johnson",
  "email": "bob.johnson@example.com",
  "password": "password456",
  "phone": "+1122334455",
  "address": "789 Pine Road, City, Country",
  "roleId": "{{roleId}}"
}

### Response Example (201 Created):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Employee created successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "employee-uuid",
###     "name": "John Doe",
###     "email": "john.doe@example.com",
###     "phone": "+1234567890",
###     "address": "123 Main Street, City, Country",
###     "roleId": "role-uuid",
###     "status": "inactive",
###     "fcmToken": null,
###     "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 2. GET ALL EMPLOYEES
### ============================================
### Get all employees with pagination and optional search/filter
### Returns employees ordered by creation date (newest first)
### Query Parameters:
###   - page: Page number (default: 1)
###   - limit: Items per page (default: 100, max: 500)
###   - search: Search term to filter by name, email, or phone (optional)
###   - status: Filter by status - active, inactive, or suspended (optional)

### Get All Employees (Default - First Page, 100 items)
GET {{baseUrl}}/employees
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Get All Employees with Pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/employees?page=1&limit=10
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Get All Employees with Search
GET {{baseUrl}}/employees?page=1&limit=10&search=john
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Get All Active Employees
GET {{baseUrl}}/employees?status=active&page=1&limit=20
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Get All Employees - Second Page
GET {{baseUrl}}/employees?page=2&limit=20
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Get All Employees with Search and Status Filter
GET {{baseUrl}}/employees?search=doe&status=active&page=1&limit=10
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Employees fetched successfully",
###   "data": [
###     {
###       "id": "employee-uuid",
###       "name": "John Doe",
###       "email": "john.doe@example.com",
###       "phone": "+1234567890",
###       "address": "123 Main Street, City, Country",
###       "roleId": "role-uuid",
###       "status": "active",
###       "fcmToken": null,
###       "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###       "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###       "Role": {
###         "id": "role-uuid",
###         "key": "admin",
###         "name": "Administrator",
###         "permissions": ["permission-uuid-1", "permission-uuid-2"]
###       }
###     }
###   ],
###   "pagination": {
###     "page": 1,
###     "limit": 10,
###     "totalPages": 5,
###     "totalItems": 50,
###     "hasNextPage": true,
###     "hasPreviousPage": false
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 3. EMPLOYEE LOGIN
### ============================================
### Login employee with email and password
### Returns JWT token for authenticated requests
### Employee must have status "active" to login
### FCM token is optional and will be updated if provided

POST {{baseUrl}}/employees/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Example: Login with FCM Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "fcmToken": "fcm-token-for-push-notifications"
}

### Response Example (200 OK):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Login successful",
###   "data": {
###     "employee": {
###       "id": "employee-uuid",
###       "name": "John Doe",
###       "email": "john.doe@example.com",
###       "phone": "+1234567890",
###       "address": "123 Main Street, City, Country",
###       "roleId": "role-uuid",
###       "status": "active",
###       "fcmToken": "fcm-token-for-push-notifications",
###       "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###       "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###       "Role": {
###         "id": "role-uuid",
###         "key": "admin",
###         "name": "Administrator",
###         "permissions": ["permission-uuid-1", "permission-uuid-2"]
###       }
###     },
###     "token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..."
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 4. UPDATE EMPLOYEE
### ============================================
### Update an existing employee
### At least one field must be provided for update
### Email and phone uniqueness is checked if being updated
### Role must exist if roleId is being updated

PUT {{baseUrl}}/employees/{{employeeId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "John Updated Doe"
}

### Example: Update Multiple Fields
PUT {{baseUrl}}/employees/{{employeeId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "John Updated Doe",
  "email": "john.updated@example.com",
  "address": "New Address, City, Country"
}

### Example: Update Status to Active
PUT {{baseUrl}}/employees/{{employeeId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "active"
}

### Example: Update Role
PUT {{baseUrl}}/employees/{{employeeId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "roleId": "{{roleId}}"
}

### Example: Update Password
PUT {{baseUrl}}/employees/{{employeeId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "password": "newpassword123"
}

### Example: Suspend Employee
PUT {{baseUrl}}/employees/{{employeeId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "suspended",
  "suspendedById": "{{employeeId}}",
  "suspendedReason": "Violation of company policy"
}

### Response Example (200 OK):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Employee updated successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "employee-uuid",
###     "name": "John Updated Doe",
###     "email": "john.updated@example.com",
###     "phone": "+1234567890",
###     "address": "New Address, City, Country",
###     "roleId": "role-uuid",
###     "status": "active",
###     "fcmToken": null,
###     "updatedById": "updater-employee-uuid",
###     "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T02:00:00.000Z",
###     "Role": {
###       "id": "role-uuid",
###       "key": "admin",
###       "name": "Administrator",
###       "permissions": ["permission-uuid-1", "permission-uuid-2"]
###     }
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### COMPREHENSIVE NOTES & GUIDELINES
### ============================================

### 1. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION
###    - Get All Employees: May require authentication (check your route configuration)
###    - Create Employee: May require authentication (check your route configuration)
###    - Update Employee: May require authentication (check your route configuration)
###    - Login: Public endpoint (no authentication required)
###    - Use the token from login response for authenticated requests
###    - Format: Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2. EMPLOYEE STATUS
###    - New employees are created with status "inactive" by default
###    - Only employees with status "active" can login
###    - Other statuses: "inactive", "suspended"
###    - To activate an employee, update their status to "active" (if update endpoint exists)

### 3. VALIDATION RULES
###    Create Employee:
###    - name: Required, string, 1-100 characters
###    - email: Required, valid email address, unique
###    - password: Required, string, 6-100 characters
###    - phone: Required, string, unique
###    - address: Required, string
###    - roleId: Required, valid UUID of existing role
###    - fcmToken: Optional, string, max 255 characters
###    - createdById: Optional, UUID of employee who created this
###    
###    Login:
###    - email: Required, valid email address
###    - password: Required, string
###    - fcmToken: Optional, string, max 255 characters
###    
###    Update Employee:
###    - At least one field must be provided
###    - name: Optional, string, 1-100 characters if provided
###    - email: Optional, valid email address if provided
###    - password: Optional, string, 6-100 characters if provided
###    - phone: Optional, string if provided
###    - address: Optional, string if provided
###    - roleId: Optional, valid UUID of existing role if provided
###    - status: Optional, enum (active, inactive, suspended) if provided
###    - fcmToken: Optional, string, max 255 characters
###    - updatedById: Optional, UUID of employee making the update
###    - suspendedById: Optional, UUID of employee who suspended this
###    - suspendedReason: Optional, string, max 500 characters

### 4. PASSWORD SECURITY
###    ⚠️  IMPORTANT: Currently passwords are stored as plain text
###    This is a security risk and should be changed to use password hashing (bcrypt, etc.)
###    The comparePassword method in the Employee model does plain text comparison

### 5. ROLE REQUIREMENTS
###    - roleId must reference an existing role in the Roles table
###    - Role information is included in login response if association is available
###    - Role permissions are included in the JWT token payload

### 6. ERROR RESPONSES
###    
###    Validation Error (400):
###    {
###      "success": false,
###      "message": "Validation error message",
###      "errors": [
###         {
###           "field": "email",
###           "message": "Email must be a valid email address"
###         }
###       ]
###     }
###    
###    Conflict (409):
###    {
###      "success": false,
###      "message": "Employee with this email already exists"
###     }
###     OR
###     {
###       "success": false,
###       "message": "Employee with this phone already exists"
###     }
###    
###    Not Found (404):
###    {
###       "success": false,
###       "message": "Role not found"
###     }
###     OR (for login/update)
###     {
###       "success": false,
###       "message": "Employee not found"
###     }
###    
###    Unauthorized (401):
###    {
###       "success": false,
###       "message": "Invalid password"
###     }
###    
###    Forbidden (403):
###    {
###       "success": false,
###       "message": "Employee account is inactive"
###     }
###     OR
###     {
###       "success": false,
###       "message": "Employee account is suspended"
###     }

### 7. SUCCESS RESPONSES
###    
###    Create Employee (201):
###    {
###       "success": true,
###       "message": "Employee created successfully",
###       "data": { ... }
###     }
###    
###    Get All Employees (200):
###    {
###       "success": true,
###       "message": "Employees fetched successfully",
###       "data": [ ... ],
###       "pagination": { ... }
###     }
###    
###    Login (200):
###    {
###       "success": true,
###       "message": "Login successful",
###       "data": {
###         "employee": { ... },
###         "token": "jwt-token-string"
###       }
###     }
###    
###    Update Employee (200):
###    {
###       "success": true,
###       "message": "Employee updated successfully",
###       "data": { ... }
###     }

### 8. JWT TOKEN PAYLOAD
###    The JWT token contains:
###    {
###       "id": "employee-uuid",
###       "email": "employee@example.com",
###       "phone": "+1234567890",
###       "name": "Employee Name",
###       "role": {
###         "id": "role-uuid",
###         "key": "admin",
###         "name": "Administrator",
###         "permissions": ["permission-uuid-1", "permission-uuid-2"]
###       },
###       "type": "employee"
###     }

### 9. BEST PRACTICES
###    - Use strong passwords (minimum 6 characters, but recommend 8+ with mixed case, numbers, symbols)
###    - Keep employee accounts inactive until they need access
###    - Update FCM tokens on login to ensure push notifications work
###    - Use HTTPS in production to protect credentials
###    - Implement password hashing before production deployment
###    - Regularly review and update employee roles and permissions

### 10. COMMON USE CASES
###    
###     Case 1: Create a new employee account
###     1. Ensure a role exists in the Roles table
###     2. POST /api/employees with employee data and roleId
###     3. Employee is created with status "inactive"
###     4. Update employee status to "active" (if update endpoint exists)
###     5. Employee can now login
###    
###     Case 2: Employee login
###     1. POST /api/employees/login with email and password
###     2. If credentials are correct and status is "active", receive JWT token
###     3. Use token for authenticated requests
###     
###     Case 3: Update FCM token on login
###     1. Include fcmToken in login request
###     2. FCM token is saved to employee record
###     3. Employee can receive push notifications
###     
###     Case 4: Get all employees with filters
###     1. GET /api/employees?status=active&search=john
###     2. Returns filtered and paginated list of employees
###     3. Use pagination to navigate through results
###     
###     Case 5: Update employee information
###     1. PUT /api/employees/:id with updated fields
###     2. Employee record is updated
###     3. Updated employee is returned with role information
###     
###     Case 6: Activate employee account
###     1. Update employee status to "active"
###     2. PUT /api/employees/:id with status: "active"
###     3. Employee can now login
###     
###     Case 7: Suspend employee account
###     1. Update employee status to "suspended"
###     2. Include suspendedById and suspendedReason
###     3. Employee cannot login until status is changed back to "active"

